  "question": {
    "text": "A bead of mass m is located on a parabolic wire with its axis vertical and vertex at the origin as shown in figure and whose equation is x<sup>2</sup> = 4ay. The wire frame is fixed and the bead can slide on it without friction. The bead is released from the point y = 4a on the wire frame from rest. The tangential acceleration of the bead when it reaches the position given by y = a is :<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0062_cb6277bee3e6.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 166px; height: 140px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mrow>  <mfrac>    <mrow>      <mtext>g</mtext>    </mrow>    <mrow>      <mn>2</mn>    </mrow>  </mfrac></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3&nbsp;</mn> </msqrt> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mrow>  <mfrac>    <mrow>      <mtext>g</mtext>    </mrow>    <mrow>      <msqrt>        <mn>5</mn>      </msqrt>    </mrow>  </mfrac></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "x<sup>2</sup> = 4ay<br /><br />Differentiating w.r.t. y, we get<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dy</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>a</mtext><br /><br />It can be considered as an inclined plane</mrow></mfrac></mrow></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0062_e9b190d59293.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 156px; height: 141px;\" /><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mtext>At</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>&nbsp;a, a</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>,</mtext> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dy</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;⇒&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> </mrow> </math>hence <math> <mrow> <mi>θ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mn>5</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />the component of weight along tangential direction is mg sin <math> <mrow> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math>.<br /><br />hence tangential acceleration is <math> <mrow> <mtext>g sin&nbsp;</mtext> <mi>θ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>"
  }
}